course: dictionary
lesson: 2801
title: Rude or respectful?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Disrespectful means rude, showing that you do not give someone the care or respect they deserve. You can be disrespectful to a person, a teacher, a place or a thing. Look at the words around it to be sure.
explain: «Interrupting the teacher and rolling your eyes is disrespectful.» Interrupting and rolling your eyes are actions that show you are not listening or caring. Disrespectful is the name for those actions. Try it: swap in rude and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Disrespectful often comes with «to» or «towards»: «It is disrespectful to call people names.» The clues show the meaning, and the word never warns you that the opposite is fine: «Asking politely is never disrespectful.» Polite asking is not rude.
fact: Disrespectful means rude and not showing respect or care for someone or something.
fact: Disrespectful is an adjective: disrespectful, more disrespectful, most disrespectful.
fact: Disrespectful can describe actions such as interrupting, calling names, ignoring teachers or damaging other people's things.
fact: «Cheeky» means rude or disrespectful, often said lightly.
fact: «Asking politely is never disrespectful» tells you that asking nicely is not rude.
exercise: «Interrupting the teacher again and again is disrespectful.» What does disrespectful mean here? | *Rude, and not showing care for the teacher | Clever and fast | Very quiet and shy | Happy and full of fun
exercise: «It is disrespectful to call people names.» Which action is disrespectful? | Helping to tidy up | *Calling a classmate a horrible name | Waiting your turn in the line | Saying please and thank you
exercise: «Asking politely is never disrespectful.» What does this sentence tell you? | Asking is always rude | Asking must always be done in a whisper | *Asking nicely is not rude | Politeness is a kind of shouting
test: «Rolling your eyes at a teacher is disrespectful.» Find and copy the one word that means rude. | eyes | rolling | *disrespectful | teacher
test: Tom says, «Cheeky means rude, said lightly.» What does cheeky mean? | *Rude or disrespectful, often said lightly | Very clever and quick | Lost in a crowd | Wet and grey
exam: Which behaviour is disrespectful? | Putting your hand up to ask a question | *Ignoring the teacher while she is speaking | Sharing your crayons | Saying thank you for the help
